<title>SOUTH AFRICA: SIMMER HALF YR SHR LOSS IMPROVES SLIGHTLY.</title>
<headline>SIMMER HALF YR SHR LOSS IMPROVES SLIGHTLY.</headline>
<dateline>JOHANNESBURG 1997-03-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>Half year ended December</p>
<p>31, 1996 </p>
<p>			(million rand unless stated)	 </p>
<p>    Shr, attrib (cts)     2.23 loss   vs 2.62 loss</p>
<p>    Attrib loss	     0.60	  vs 0.71</p>
<p>    Net finance charges   0.12	  vs 0.03 income</p>
<p>    Operating loss	  0.48	  vs 0.74</p>
<p>    Operating costs	 7.19	  vs 6.40</p>
<p>    Turnover		  6.70	  vs 5.66</p>
<p>Full name: Simmer and Jack Mines Ltd </p>
<p>NOTE - Directors said funding of the losses and exploration</p>
<p>activities had been secured by way of existing bank facilities</p>
<p>which are considered adequate to meet commitments as they fall</p>
<p>due.</p>
<p>-- Johannesburg newsroom +27 11 482 1003</p>
</text>
